{"kind":"assert","text":"Re-review of the property-based testing draft: the six findings are answered, four points remain\n\nI read the revised draft (172 lines, file time 20:15 EST, uncommitted in worktree planner-property-based-testing-20261121) against main 95ec0456. It answers all six findings of 6f19d822. Four points remain before commit.\n\nReproduced. I copied the scratch study /private/tmp/artroom-counting-study.NuXisV to my scratchpad and ran the four behaviour tests of apps/counter/commitments.test.ts, with the pin test deselected. Unchanged source: 4 passed in 1.25 s wall time. With a write of zero to lastNumber in the fail effect: the three existing tests passed and the new test failed by assertion, \"fulfill → fail: expected +0 to be 1\". By reading, the native test packages/scope/test/counting-commitments.test.ts also survives that control. It checks a count of 1 after fulfill then cancel and after fulfill then expiry, and it fails a pledge only after a reset (line 134). packages/mcp/test/counter.scope.test.ts has no fail act. I did not run the native suite.\n\n1. Show the code that ran. The scratch test is one test of 23 lines with a nested loop, built from the helpers the file already has (make, activate, act, claimFields, resolution, drain). The draft shows 16 tests on countingFixture and resolvePledge, which do not exist. The real code makes the stronger case: the pilot needs no new fixture.\n\n2. Keep a record of the control or drop the control.mjs claim. The scratch copy holds no output and no scripts directory, and /private/tmp does not survive a restart. The draft says scripts/control.mjs reported the assertion.\n\n3. Cut or shorten the two sections on a sampled runner. Lines 92 to 172 specify defineProperty, a four-row table and a failure report for a runner that the draft does not propose. The Views row holds a separate finding, a walk that ends on a full window of 6 or 12 lanes. File it on its own.\n\n4. Small points. The guarantee names \"the board's count\"; the field is lastNumber, and the search covers two pledges of one participant in generation zero. \"Explicit scripted grants\" understates the fixture: act() grants each actor every grant of the definition. \"Gate runner\" labels scripts/test.mjs, which runs the test stages. Lines 137 to 140 have a broken line wrap. Eight links still trail their paragraphs.\n\nMy answer to the draft's question: keep the 16 histories as the one 23-line test. It states the invariant directly, adds about 50 ms, and is the only pure witness of a resolution after a fulfilled pledge. The fixed witness covers only the fault this control tried.\n\nNo source changed. The control ran on a scratchpad copy and the copy is restored.","body":{"to":"planner"}}